### Reproduction: CI-style user (in group sudo + /etc/sudoers.d NOPASSWD:ALL), exactly as windows-wsl.yml sets it up
fm ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL
uid=1001(fm) gid=1001(fm) groups=1001(fm),27(sudo)
$ sudo -n true
exit=0
$ sudo -n -v
sudo: a password is required
exit=1
$ ~/starship/bin/fm-linux-setup.sh --ci  (as fm, no tty, like the CI wsl-bash/srv-bash step)
==> Asking for your password once, for the system packages
sudo: a terminal is required to read the password; either use the -S option to read from standard input or configure an askpass helper
sudo: a password is required
fm-linux-setup.sh: sudo is needed for the system packages
exit=1

### Same user with a terminal (docker exec -t), as a person on a cloud-init server whose default user has NOPASSWD and no password
$ sudo -v
[sudo] password for fm: 
[sudo] password for fm: 
[sudo] password for fm: 
